{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender CMake Build System.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender CMake Build System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender cmake build system blender cmake build system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender CMake Build System.md","fileName":"Blender CMake Build System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender CMake Build System","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Core Source Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Core Source Architecture","Blender Module Build Option","Blender Debug Build Configuration","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender CMake Build System.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender CMake Build System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender cmake build system blender cmake build system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender CMake Build System.md","fileName":"Blender CMake Build System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender CMake Build System","heading":"Blender CMake Build System","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender uses CMake as a meta-build system that generates platform-specific projects or scripts for environments such as Visual Studio and Make. A top-level `CMakeLists.txt` establishes global configuration, while nested build files describe core directories, individual modules, and supporting scripts.\n\nThis hierarchy lets one source tree target several operating systems and build tools. `add_subdirectory()` assembles modules, variables configure dependencies, and the [[Blender Module Build Option]] can remove optional capabilities. A [[Blender Debug Build Configuration]] then changes how the resulting program supports inspection and tracing.","tags":["baby"],"link